# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 82-86 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 11 — CHAPTER 13, 2026-09-21; the one run): the header (82), the prophet (83-84), the six
# verbs (85), the prophet's death (86) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files (the whole-row rule); every quotation of the shelf CUT by consonants (ch13_ink.SP_ —
# a miss lands in FAIL, asserted empty by the ledger writer); a middah named only where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md, the code checked before it is
# typed); the rows read before at earlier sittings marked REREAD WHOLE. Speed ruling (c): CONTEXT rows terse. Chapter 12's form (ch12_rows_sifrei_59_62.py).
from ch13_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(82, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ALL THE WORD THAT I COMMAND YOU" (13:1) — THAT A LIGHT COMMANDMENT BE AS DEAR TO YOU AS A WEIGHTY ONE. The head row of piska 82, THE FIRST ON THE CHAPTER ({SP_(82, 1, "שתהא", "מצוה", "קלה", "חביבה")} "that a light commandment be dear"): the header\'s "all the word" read as the whole law weighed alike (Mishnah Avot 2:1 the English\'s note; 79:2 the same on 12:28) — THE INK: "all the word that I command you" ONE seat in the Bible; 4:2\'s plural clause its twin, seven tokens in order (computed). Fresh.')
srow(82, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"IT YOU SHALL KEEP TO DO" — R. ELIEZER SON OF JACOB: TO SET A PROHIBITION ON EVERY POSITIVE COMMAND SAID IN THE PASSAGE. ({SP_(82, 2, "לתן", "לא", "תעשה", "על", "כל", "עשה")} "to set a prohibition on every positive command"): "keep" the prohibition\'s word, "do" the command\'s — the compile\'s rule that a prescription carries its proscription (85:3 says it of the six verbs). Fresh.')
srow(82, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT ADD TO IT NOR TAKE FROM IT" — FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH ZEVACHIM 8:10): BLOODS GIVEN IN ONE APPLICATION THAT MIXED WITH BLOODS GIVEN IN ONE APPLICATION ARE GIVEN IN ONE; the English supplies Tosefta Zevachim 8:23 in brackets — the four-application blood mixed with the one-application blood: R. Eliezer four (else "do not take away"), R. Joshua one (else "do not add"). ({SP_(82, 3, "הנתנים", "במתנה", "אחת", "שנתערבו")} "those given in one application that mixed"): THE VERSE READ AS A TWO-SIDED GATE on the altar\'s rite — each side cited against the other (the English\'s bracketed Tosefta not the Hebrew row\'s); the answer sheet Mishnah Zevachim 8:10, routed to 11b\'s docket. Fresh.')
srow(82, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "YOU SHALL NOT ADD TO IT" — WHENCE THAT ONE ADDS NOT TO THE LULAV (THE PALM BRANCH\'S FOUR SPECIES) NOR TO THE FRINGES? "YOU SHALL NOT ADD." WHENCE THAT ONE TAKES NOT FROM THEM? "NOR TAKE FROM IT." ({SP_(82, 4, "שאין", "מוסיפים", "על", "הלולב", "ועל", "הציצית")} "that one does not add to the palm branch nor to the fringes"): THE COUNT AS A PARAMETER WITH BOTH EDGES BARRED — four species, four fringes (the English\'s notes: Mishnah Sukkah 3:7-14, Tosefta Sukkah 2:8 the measures). Fresh.')
srow(82, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT IF A PRIEST BEGAN THE PRIESTLY BLESSING HE SHALL NOT SAY "SINCE I HAVE BEGUN, I WILL ADD \'THE LORD THE GOD OF YOUR FATHERS ADD TO YOU\' (1:11)"? "THE WORD" — EVEN A WORD YOU SHALL NOT ADD. ({SP_(82, 5, "אפלו", "דבר", "לא", "תוסף", "עליו")} "even a word you shall not add to it"): the header\'s noun read at its grain — a WORD; 1:11\'s blessing (read at sitting 1) the case. REREAD WHOLE (sitting 1).')

srow(83, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN A PROPHET ARISES AMONG YOU" (13:2) — AS MOSES SPOKE WITH "THUS SAID", SO THE PROPHETS; AS MOSES SAID PART AND FULFILLED PART, SO THE PROPHETS; AS MOSES SPOKE A GENERAL RULE AND A PARTICULAR, SO THE PROPHETS; OR AS MOSES WAS OLD, EIGHTY, THE SON OF AMRAM — MIGHT THE PROPHETS BE SO TOO? "A PROPHET" — IN ANY CASE. The head row of piska 83 ({SP_(83, 1, "נביא", "מכל", "מקום")} "a prophet — in any case"): THE PROPHET\'S FORMS TAKEN FROM MOSES\' — the formula, the partial fulfilment, the general-and-particular — and his person not: the compile\'s parameter for what a claim of prophecy is (the run\'s "thus said the LORD" at Exodus 5:1 cited by the English). Fresh.')
srow(83, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"OR A DREAMER OF A DREAM" — SINCE IT IS SAID OF MOSES "MOUTH TO MOUTH I SPEAK WITH HIM" (NUMBERS 12:8), MIGHT THE PROPHETS BE SO? "OR A DREAMER OF A DREAM." ({SP_(83, 2, "פה", "אל", "פה", "אדבר", "בו")} "mouth to mouth I speak with him"): the dream the prophets\' channel, not Moses\' (Numbers 12:6-8 read at its sitting). Fresh.')
srow(83, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AMONG YOU" — TO INCLUDE THE WOMAN. ({SP_(83, 3, "לרבות", "את", "האשה")} "to include the woman"). Fresh.')
srow(83, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND GIVES YOU A SIGN" — IN THE HEAVENS; SO IT SAYS "AND THEY SHALL BE FOR SIGNS" (GENESIS 1:14). ({SP_(83, 4, "בשמים")} "in the heavens"): the lights\' word. REREAD WHOLE (a Genesis sitting).')
srow(83, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"A WONDER" — ON THE EARTH; SO IT SAYS "IF THERE BE DEW ON THE FLEECE ALONE" (JUDGES 6:37) — "AND GOD DID SO" (6:40). ({SP_(83, 5, "בארץ")} "on the earth"): Gideon\'s fleece the wonder\'s case. Fresh.')

srow(84, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE SIGN AND THE WONDER COME TO PASS" (13:3) — R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: SEE HOW FAR THE TEXT GOES — IN THE END THE IDOLATERS ARE GIVEN DOMINION EVEN OVER THE SUN AND THE MOON, THE STARS AND THE CONSTELLATIONS; DO NOT HEARKEN TO THEM! WHY? "FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD IS TESTING YOU." The head row of piska 84 ({SP_(84, 1, "אפלו", "על", "חמה", "ולבנה")} "even over the sun and the moon"): THE SIGN GRANTED TRUE and the hearing barred anyway — the test the reason. Fresh.')
srow(84, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: HEAVEN FORBID THAT THE OMNIPRESENT STOP THE SUN, THE MOON, THE STARS FOR IDOLATERS! THE TEXT SPEAKS ONLY OF THOSE WHO WERE TRUE PROPHETS AT FIRST AND TURNED TO BE FALSE PROPHETS, LIKE HANANIAH SON OF AZZUR. ({SP_(84, 2, "כחנניה", "בן", "עזור")} "like Hananiah son of Azzur"): THE DISPUTE ON THE SIGN — a real wonder given to a seducer (R. Yose) against a former true prophet\'s standing (R. Akiva; Jeremiah 28 the run\'s case, 189:1 its "rebellion"): the compile\'s PARAMETER for the sign\'s status. Fresh.')
srow(84, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOU SHALL NOT HEARKEN TO THE WORDS OF THAT PROPHET" (13:4) — AND NOT ONE WHO RETRACTS. ({SP_(84, 3, "ולא", "החוזר", "בו")} "and not one who retracts"). Fresh.')
srow(84, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"OR TO THAT DREAMER OF THE DREAM" — AND NOT ONE SUSPECTED IN HINDSIGHT. ({SP_(84, 4, "ולא", "החשוד", "למפרע")} "and not one suspected retroactively"). Fresh.')
srow(84, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD IS TESTING YOU TO KNOW WHETHER YOU LOVE" — the verse cited whole, no gloss ({SP_(84, 5, "כי", "מנסה")} "for … is testing"). Fresh.')

srow(85, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AFTER THE LORD YOUR GOD YOU SHALL WALK" (13:5) — THIS IS THE CLOUD. The head row of piska 85 ({SP_(85, 1, "זה", "הענן")} "this is the cloud"): the first of the six verbs made a RUN CITATION — the march after the cloud (Numbers 9:15-23, 10:11-12 on the tape) the walking after Him. Fresh.')
srow(85, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND HIM YOU SHALL FEAR" — THAT HIS FEAR BE UPON YOU. ({SP_(85, 2, "שיהא", "מוראו", "עליכם")} "that His fear be upon you"): Onkelos\'s supplement the same word. Fresh.')
srow(85, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HIS COMMANDMENTS" — THIS IS THE POSITIVE COMMAND; "YOU SHALL KEEP" — TO SET A PROHIBITION. ({SP_(85, 3, "זו", "מצות", "עשה")} "this is the positive command"; {SP_(85, 3, "לתן", "לא", "תעשה")} "to set a prohibition"): 82:2\'s rule at the six verbs — "keep" the prohibition\'s verb. Fresh.')
srow(85, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HIS VOICE YOU SHALL OBEY" — THE VOICE OF HIS PROPHETS. ({SP_(85, 4, "בקול", "נביאיו")} "the voice of His prophets"): the true prophet\'s authority (18:15\'s "to him you shall hearken", ahead) seated inside the false prophet\'s chapter — the obedience commanded here is the very channel 13:2-4 tests. Fresh.')
srow(85, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND HIM YOU SHALL SERVE" — SERVE HIM IN HIS TORAH, SERVE HIM IN HIS SANCTUARY. ({SP_(85, 5, "עבדו", "בתורתו", "עבדו", "במקדשו")} "serve Him in His Torah, serve Him in His sanctuary"). Fresh.')
srow(85, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND TO HIM YOU SHALL CLEAVE" — SEPARATE FROM IDOLATRY AND CLEAVE TO THE OMNIPRESENT. ({SP_(85, 6, "הפרשו", "מעבודה", "זרה")} "separate from idolatry"): the cleaving the chapter\'s counter-verb (13:18 the devoted thing not cleaving). Fresh.')

srow(86, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THAT PROPHET" (13:6) — AND NOT ONE COERCED. The head row of piska 86 ({SP_(86, 1, "ולא", "אנוס")} "and not one coerced"). Fresh.')
srow(86, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"OR THAT DREAMER OF THE DREAM" — AND NOT ONE MISLED. ({SP_(86, 2, "ולא", "מטעה")} "and not one misled"): the exemptions of duress and error — the exam\'s persons. Fresh.')
srow(86, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"SHALL BE PUT TO DEATH, FOR HE SPOKE REBELLION AGAINST THE LORD YOUR GOD" — IS IT NOT AN A FORTIORI: IF ONE WHO FALSIFIES HIS FELLOW\'S WORDS IS LIABLE TO DEATH, ONE WHO FALSIFIES THE WORDS OF THE OMNIPRESENT HOW MUCH MORE! ({SP_(86, 3, "והלא", "דברים", "קל", "וחומר")} "is it not an a fortiori"): I1 (checked) from the plotting witness (Mishnah Makkot 1:4-6 the English\'s note — 19:16-19\'s law, ahead) to the false prophet — the death given a reason. Fresh.')
srow(86, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHO BROUGHT YOU OUT OF THE LAND OF EGYPT" — EVEN HAD HE NO CLAIM ON YOU BUT THAT HE BROUGHT YOU OUT OF EGYPT, ENOUGH. ({SP_(86, 4, "אפלו", "אין", "לו", "עליך", "אלא")} "even had He no claim on you but"): the exodus the sufficient claim (90:3 says it again at 13:11). Fresh.')
srow(86, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND REDEEMED YOU FROM THE HOUSE OF BONDAGE" — EVEN HAD HE NO CLAIM BUT THAT HE REDEEMED YOU FROM THE HOUSE OF BONDAGE, ENOUGH. ({SP_(86, 5, "שפדאך", "מבית", "עבדים")} "that He redeemed you from the house of bondage"): the two clauses two claims. Fresh.')
srow(86, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THRUST YOU FROM THE WAY" — "THRUSTING" IS SAID HERE AND "THRUSTING" IS SAID BELOW (13:11): AS THE THRUSTING BELOW IS BY STONING, SO THE THRUSTING HERE IS BY STONING. R. SHIMON: THIS ONE\'S DEATH IS ONLY BY STRANGLING. ({SP_(86, 6, "נאמר", "כאן", "הדחה", "ונאמרה", "להלן")} "thrusting is said here and thrusting is said below"; {SP_(86, 6, "בחנק")} "by strangling"): I2 (checked) on the chapter\'s own verb — the prophet\'s bare "shall be put to death" GIVEN ITS MODE from the inciter\'s stoning; THE DISPUTE (stoning / strangling — Mishnah Sanhedrin 11:1\'s strangled prophet at 11b) a PARAMETER of the death. Fresh.')
srow(86, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "FROM THE WAY" — THIS IS THE POSITIVE COMMAND. ({SP_(86, 7, "זו", "מצות", "עשה")} "this is the positive command"). Fresh.')
srow(86, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD COMMANDED YOU" — THIS IS THE PROHIBITION. ({SP_(86, 8, "זו", "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "this is the prohibition"): the way\'s two halves. Fresh.')
srow(86, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO WALK IN IT" — NOT ONE WHO SAYS PART AND LEAVES PART. ({SP_(86, 9, "לא", "האומר", "מקצת", "ומשיר", "מקצת")} "not one who says part and leaves part"): the seducer who uproots part of the way (Tosefta Sanhedrin 14:13 the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(86, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL PURGE THE EVIL FROM YOUR MIDST" — PURGE THE DOER OF EVILS FROM ISRAEL. ({SP_(86, 10, "בער", "עושה", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doer of evils from Israel"): THE FORMULA\'S FIRST SEAT (13:6 — nine in the Bible, all in the book, computed) read as the PERSON removed, not the deed — the compile\'s effect: the execution purges. Fresh.')

assert sorted(S) == [(82, r) for r in range(1, 6)] + [(83, r) for r in range(1, 6)] + [(84, r) for r in range(1, 6)] + [(85, r) for r in range(1, 7)] + [(86, r) for r in range(1, 11)], sorted(S)
